    <dialog id="about-dialog" aria-labelledby="about-heading"><div class="dialog-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Read the map</p><h2 id="about-heading">Many futures.<br />A shared atlas.</h2></div><form method="dialog"><button class="dialog-close" aria-label="Close about">×</button></form></div><p class="dialog-intro">The Atlas of Contested Futures connects public research, people and events around the futures we imagine, debate and build.</p><div class="about-grid"><section><h3>Begin anywhere</h3><p>Select a collection, search for an idea, or follow a node. Every loaded record is submitted as its own point. Zoom changes the view, not a sample. Names are an optional, separate layer of catalog-local labels. Positions and overlapping theme regions are illustrative. Labels are limited for readability; point and route data are not sampled. The reading room searches every record.</p></section><section><h3>Read connections carefully</h3><p>Credits connect catalog-local name labels to records. Record links include source-listed relationships and editorial related-article cards, not necessarily body citations. Dashed lines identify inferred matches. Select two territories to compare their records and inspect the exact source evidence. Cyan credits and green recorded links flow faster; violet inferred matches and amber title themes flow slower. Speed indicates evidence category, not a numerical probability. Paired movement implies no causal direction. Pause motion stops the flow. Themes come from overlapping English title-keyword matches; unmatched records remain searchable. A connection never implies agreement or endorsement.</p></section><section><h3>A map with open edges</h3><p>The initial collection draws on public IEET and separately collected related catalogs. Historical coverage is incomplete. Some dates and bylines are missing; possible duplicates and name ambiguities remain. Each record keeps its source evidence.</p></section><section><h3>Public by design</h3><p>The opening riddle is playful, not authentication. This site contains public metadata and links, not private research notes or full copyrighted articles. Additional catalogs are imported locally in your browser.</p></section></div><a class="source-link" href="/ACF/coverage.json" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Collection coverage and provenance <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></dialog>
